  {
   "version": "0.6.0",
   "tag": "v0.6.0",
   "date": "2026-10-23",
   "page": "https://github.com/Xaxis/brickworks/releases/tag/v0.6.0",
   "notes": "https://github.com/Xaxis/brickworks/blob/v0.6.0/CHANGELOG.md",
   "summary": "A release about big models and what holds them. View > Stress tints every part by how near its weakest joint is to letting go, and flags only a joint that really is weak: on eight real sets that stand, one part reads red, a 9 g branch on one stud. A big model opens without freezing the window, and Timeline on one no longer pauses. Turning a model's moving parts by hand is lighter, most of all on a phone. A part laid at an angle is held by the studs it sits on, so the tow truck's fifth wheel turns on its axle. Claude finds a part by the words a builder uses for it, and never offers a place for a part that it then refuses. On brickworks.diy the gallery, model pages and profiles are new, with a feed, comments in threads and notifications. Models saved by 0.5.0 open in 0.6.0 unchanged.",
