  {
   "version": "0.5.0",
   "tag": "v0.5.0",
   "date": "2026-10-22",
   "page": "https://github.com/Xaxis/brickworks/releases/tag/v0.5.0",
   "notes": "https://github.com/Xaxis/brickworks/blob/v0.5.0/CHANGELOG.md",
   "summary": "A release about opening and moving real models. File > Library\u2026 opens any of 1,575 models of real LEGO\u00ae sets and their alternate builds, from LDraw's Official Model Repository, each with its cover, its builder credited and its licence, in a tab of its own; the gallery's shared models are a shelf beside them. Grab turns 85 of the repository's sets by their steering as the real ones turn, where 0.4.0 turned 59: universal joints bend, racks keep their pinions, a loop comes back where it began, and a hinge turns as far as its parts let it. My Claude designs a new model twice, side by side, and keeps the better, and Undo takes back all of a session's first design. The window no longer stops while Claude moves a part or checks a design. Brickify lays more of a model's steep sides on their sides, and the undersides of overhangs in slopes you can buy. Claude's domes of hinged panels build again, and a second design in one chat keeps its own subject. Models saved by 0.4.0 open in 0.5.0 unchanged.",
